## Commit Rules

`Write` operations targeting files under `preparation/`, `execution/`, `analysis/` and `report/` trigger an individual best-effort auto-commit through the PostToolUse hook. `Edit` operations and files outside those directories are not covered. At completion, stage and commit any remaining approved work once. Push only through the confirmation provided by `/wrap-session`.

## Compaction

When `/compact` fires, preserve:
- The current pipeline/stage identifier and active working directory (which section, which stage, which command is mid-run).
- Paths to any subagent-output files the main session has not yet read.
- Any pending operator gate the session is holding at.

Auto-compact drops these by priority; name them explicitly so they survive.
